From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] iokit: build NeoDarwin's generic Arm platform expert

On a machine whose device tree root is "NeoDarwin,sbsa" no platform
expert matched and IOPanicPlatform panicked ("Unable to find driver for
this platform"). Apple's ARM platform experts, interrupt controllers and
power managers are closed kexts. NeoDarwin's (kernel/neodarwin/platform,
overlaid at iokit/ndplatform) are compiled into the kernel, as
AppleARMSMP.cpp is:
- NeoDarwinPlatformExpert, an IODTPlatformExpert;
- NeoDarwinGICv3, the IRQ interrupt controller and IPIs;
- NeoDarwinPSCI, the IOPMGR.

This patch lists them for arm64 and adds the built-in personality that
matches the platform expert to the device tree root.

Rebase-risk: low (appended entries).
---
--- a/iokit/conf/files.arm64	2026-09-28 10:28:52
+++ b/iokit/conf/files.arm64	2026-09-28 10:28:52
@@ -6,5 +6,10 @@
 # SMP
 iokit/Kernel/arm/AppleARMSMP.cpp    					optional iokitcpp
 
+# NeoDarwin generic Arm platform: expert, GICv3, PSCI (kernel/neodarwin/platform)
+iokit/ndplatform/NeoDarwinPlatformExpert.cpp	optional iokitcpp
+iokit/ndplatform/NeoDarwinGICv3.cpp	optional iokitcpp
+iokit/ndplatform/NeoDarwinPSCI.cpp	optional iokitcpp
+
 # tightbeamc generated implementation files
 ./Exclaves/IOService.tightbeam.c		optional iokitcpp config_exclaves
--- a/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp	2026-09-28 10:28:52
+++ b/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp	2026-09-28 10:28:52
@@ -40,6 +40,12 @@
     "     'IOProbeScore'    = 0:32;"
     "   },"
     "   {"
+    "     'IOClass'         = NeoDarwinPlatformExpert;"
+    "     'IOProviderClass' = IOPlatformExpertDevice;"
+    "     'IONameMatch'     = 'NeoDarwin,sbsa';"
+    "     'IOProbeScore'    = 1000:32;"
+    "   },"
+    "   {"
     "     'IOClass'         = IOExclaveProxy;"
     "     'IOProviderClass' = IOService;"
     "     'IOExclaveProxy'  = 1:32;"
